# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The .env line is not housekeeping. `next build` copies the project's .env into
# .next/standalone, and the generated server.js loads it — so a .env in the
# context does not merely sit in an intermediate layer, it is carried into the
# final image and overrides the environment the container is given, with this
# machine's AUTH_SECRET and SECRETS_KEY in it. The Dockerfile deletes those
# files again in the runner stage, so it takes both of these going wrong.
#
# The rest is size: the context is sent to the daemon before anything runs, and
# node_modules is most of a gigabyte the build discards immediately.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
.next
.git
.github

test-results
playwright-report
e2e

npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
